      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That's a very real and heavy feeling, and it makes sense that it scares you. But a void isn't the absence of life—it's the space where something new has to be built, even if it doesn't feel like it yet. You're not a hollow shell; you're a person in the middle of a transformation that hasn't shown its shape yet. The fact that you can name this emptiness so clearly means you're still very much here, still searching. And that searching, even when it feels like drowning, is proof that the story isn't over.",
